<title>INDIA: First lady director elected to India's BSE.</title>
<headline>First lady director elected to India's BSE.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE), India premier bourse, elected its first lady director on Thursday, the exchange said.</p>
<p>Deena Mehta was one of four brokers elected to the board of the BSE which was founded in 1875, it said.</p>
<p>Mahendra Kampani, Anand Rathi and Ramesh Damani were the other three brokers elected to the 19-member board.</p>
<p>The board has nine elected brokers with another nine as nominated public representatives. The executive director is appointed by the federal government.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
